[{"id":"VRCE-3-23-1","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":23,"verse":1,"english":"When Khara of fierce prowess had come to the asylum Rāma in company with his brother saw all those evil prognostics.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-24-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3023001","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a6770c0b1f0971ca73cf0f4ac80163a3a9f3abaddaabcce816066d55bbdf9b35","compact":"3a2a669b1eab48775c0ee2d993e3668b8e19135b33a5e09e76472e1ddf750f68","nasal":"3a2a669b1eab48775c0ee2d993e3668b8e19135b33a5e09e76472e1ddf750f68"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-23-2","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":23,"verse":2,"english":"And beholding those dreadful portents, Rāma exceedingly distressed, apprehending some calamity to the Rākşasas, observed to Lakşmaņa.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.658,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-24-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3023002","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"aacc10b0a69db74a8747e2f383ff1144078f666469f8d2ece4a74715ec7fe238","compact":"cd140f1f4a8898791452e70f5e1427b50b6c818a2cb8ddc274922a774bacc384","nasal":"18a35e656828bb15cc72c7646abd3ed97076aa60aa6f9bbd3949f03df09b859d"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-23-3","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":23,"verse":3,"english":"O mighty armed one, behold these great presages that have taken place, capable of annihilating all beings, and which have taken place, capable of annihilating all beings, and which have for their object the utter extermination of the Raksasas!","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-24-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3023003","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"83f24a48275d0cda008cb880b15c6df42fb64e035c63c52e34a7e352d2755602","compact":"d068a40192d0272e75859d52e081e5cc6687d89d3b174800fe8cb88dda3a00cc","nasal":"d068a40192d0272e75859d52e081e5cc6687d89d3b174800fe8cb88dda3a00cc"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-23-4","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":23,"verse":4,"english":"Yonder threatening clouds of asinine sable, showering down blood and uttering loud sounds are ranging the welkin.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.508,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-24-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3023004","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b5b616ec5f8717be0769e0e5245ad9c3486542464e5554d0730fe84fdfc60875","compact":"6c5b0763dfc3a8ebb67645560288886db5002a983af97f2b544f7f21d32edc14","nasal":"84d4863fca4caa2cee1e0515de8aaad7e504eae09ed7f5821aa5c370c5d37acd"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-23-5","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":23,"verse":5,"english":"And, O discerning one, rejoicing at the prospect of my fight, all these arrows emit smoke, and my bows plaited on the back with gold, are restless.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.631,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-24-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3023005","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"514470bfa242525c20d952b927776ca9712b728088f847baa47c6fcfc59886e8","compact":"9afdfea188476ffc432eb2938a7a3008e668466fa6af80c7a0530f03540ee1ab","nasal":"373f2c06dc8d387bfa4299060bb24f87730bc9c5a5ca0558b98200a34f31cc56"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-23-6","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":23,"verse":6,"english":"Meseems from the noise of the wild birds that impending on us is danger and uncertainty to life.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.857,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-24-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3023006","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"79b5521d3f59b6d394b287e5f230b6fa93f182a668890bab020eb2879a265b06","compact":"88c0da83e109aafedd58af9303e14c8c9551899fced2d7c95621f962c3e20d99","nasal":"b98ba69b512d0cd31db99e8c364896bb27d3c1e9b09565f01754211f35e43890"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-23-7","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":23,"verse":7,"english":"Without doubt, there shall take place a mighty conflict. At this critical time, my arin shaking momentarily, betokens, O hero, victory to us, and defeat to the enemy. And your face appear pleasant with a delightful lustre.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.968,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-24-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3023007","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"88ab0f5b69b70172d8a7ccc2f861ce2f9c7e117d0cb08b0e06ec40bd072e357a","compact":"9a033d7ed1addef3fe9dd90019d19c95fee2579f8f9baca58ac38ca62da7acb5","nasal":"9a033d7ed1addef3fe9dd90019d19c95fee2579f8f9baca58ac38ca62da7acb5"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-23-8","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":23,"verse":8,"english":"Without doubt, there shall take place a mighty conflict. At this critical time, my arin shaking momentarily, betokens, O hero, victory to us, and defeat to the enemy. And your face appear pleasant with a delightful lustre.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-24-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3023008","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3f6ea8aa978ac67791235230a36554d10004cf32081cb9bc2a5fb6b34cf019fa","compact":"8f71b633870663a3d8343544e1cf42786ded737b8e3410aa8a1c70ff8cba1418","nasal":"fef3f83883b9ce98886ae43347e5679af1facfd42b029b04cd5201be4bd8cb31"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-23-9","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":23,"verse":9,"english":"O Lakşmaņa, the pallid face of those that prepare for conflict, auger shortening of life.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.879,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-24-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3023009","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c32c5f43b58811d4eaa707f0d2c9f6ad58702a54bbee348aa0bbed13b9446c0f","compact":"4af96d597768ca838d769045df6bd21591288a423bd7cf4cce0ca84684ce830b","nasal":"4af96d597768ca838d769045df6bd21591288a423bd7cf4cce0ca84684ce830b"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-23-10","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":23,"verse":10,"english":"A considerate person that wishes for his welfare, apprehending peril, should prevent disaster ere it arrives.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-24-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3023010","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ec963c2ba54107e83076410156f3290ea486c778d752a5ff7375122b2b8cca2c","compact":"f7cb886be529cee34c0a5f744bfc9d37520302e709fcc459268d8c7ea456db6f","nasal":"db7c63b5687f7dadd83a7c7af150d7ee814eed0c8de2d437e590c6adf78b6cfe"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-23-11","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":23,"verse":11,"english":"Therefore bearing arrows in your hand, and equipped with your bow, do you, taking Videha's daughter, take refuge in the mountain cavern, covered with trees and difficult of access.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.864,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-24-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3023011","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"764dbd5511e8d5d0b9ba63aa06271685c3fd875e30494c181dd8154622acdece","compact":"ccab9875fd1db48259d5012b0a5a6d564e9331183831e67897d1f7002bc8a2af","nasal":"ccab9875fd1db48259d5012b0a5a6d564e9331183831e67897d1f7002bc8a2af"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-23-12","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":23,"verse":12,"english":"That you should act contrary to my words, is what I do not wish. Swearing by my feet, go you without delay, my brother.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-24-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3023012","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"123defd27751b73f6012ae992da15cced2a18d084724217c12022cdff31705fb","compact":"5fd4151175de325cdb81e6c477df3b6945f2752c849bf152c453b4705cbffcd1","nasal":"5fd4151175de325cdb81e6c477df3b6945f2752c849bf152c453b4705cbffcd1"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-23-13","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":23,"verse":13,"english":"Thus accosted by Rama, Laksmana, taking arrows and a bow, took refuge in an inaccessible cave along with Sītā.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.862,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-24-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3023013","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6de24e4bdb7bdf6adf95a336622285f88f75acbab3dc882c9367c1b4ffe49be8","compact":"82a5d428a56c5102f109f3cdd851ab16e1c81f28908d2188a79b09f620181b46","nasal":"82a5d428a56c5102f109f3cdd851ab16e1c81f28908d2188a79b09f620181b46"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-23-14","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":23,"verse":14,"english":"Thereupon, saying, Ah! we have spoken it sharp, Rāma put on his mail. And adorned with that mail resembling fire Rāma appeared in the dark like a mighty flame streaming up.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.9,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-24-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3023014","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b3ded0660fb2198576e1508191ec2d51a904c347eaa5ba2b401edde79053d8f5","compact":"63971d298c606fb092d88440cf5e88eb1d562830caedaf3451aa309c95ca3e66","nasal":"b15a8f589f636faf86524d93d0dcbb68e8e76b9762c04e339533ee3533874aa1"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-23-15","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":23,"verse":15,"english":"Thereupon, saying, Ah! we have spoken it sharp, Rāma put on his mail. And adorned with that mail resembling fire Rāma appeared in the dark like a mighty flame streaming up.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.741,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-24-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3023015","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a049c9090315fce810f4d28a71ca2500340674c9460523598938940a0bebc9c1","compact":"ab336794e9c506e39a25958130f65b050050abec4a557de67c8d2dbabb28e3e7","nasal":"ab336794e9c506e39a25958130f65b050050abec4a557de67c8d2dbabb28e3e7"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-23-16","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":23,"verse":16,"english":"And uplifting his bow, and taking his arrows, that powerful one stood there, feeling all directions with the twangs of his bow-string.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.794,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-24-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3023016","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"eccb3309af80b115a69cf9c4d5c5bf2bb491f3d0d936af21166ea9d8af824055","compact":"e77a8eadbdd5021d997cf7500ac7e6c5d67663a41cdc877be5d7d15d7dd6d70a","nasal":"5ee2d5a3bdc51b55fb486d19f81c74f6fecb78981f6f4dd56424f98c71de1f05"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-23-17","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":23,"verse":17,"english":"Then the high-souled gods and Gandharvas, Siddhas and Cāranas came there, with the intention of witnessing the fight.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.452,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-24-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3023017","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6cbc62a5c50ddfb0a36c85c58d3f40c3f94eb455993a76075743aa5f1e02a7fd","compact":"14ade5dc41180d5d3440a693d6eb8ece3aa625c6a7365660897a7f0ca9c7391a","nasal":"710a393953a0987bee95c7e0a49714084f3b2c4f0ad9c0bc5facfba073c0c69e"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-23-18","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":23,"verse":18,"english":"Having said this, they again spoke, eyeing one another, There are fourteen thousand of the Rākşasas of dreadful deed while the righteous Rāma is single. How can fight take place (between two such parties)?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-24-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3023018","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"426eb168ab38aed9e5ec286989a2b627dc868152e8f9c6c19d2c5b380f1999c0","compact":"934ee2638537ce8d5b3eec5f41a81ce7f67c3ce6823fdb761b03970bb245a0b5","nasal":"934ee2638537ce8d5b3eec5f41a81ce7f67c3ce6823fdb761b03970bb245a0b5"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-23-19","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":23,"verse":19,"english":"While the gods, Gandharvas and Cāraņas were thus conversing, the forces of the Rākṣasas sending up solemn sounds, furnished with horrible armour, arms and flags, conversing in heroic parlance, roaring at each other, stretching bows, momentarily yawning, sending forth shouts, and blowing trumpets. The commentator says the yawning was in consequence of the soldiers having during the conflict indulged in liquor.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.615,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-24-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3023019","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"36c252375309ba5c5d19e9c160f57fd8f7778a2e03e01699820de46060523590","compact":"f804f2becbd7650570af0d57438f3a23cd6709ba406b6d54b5fbf77130832990","nasal":"a33bc83d294a7035d5f3a6e2bfa4ee09461d5b023c0774b462a2b5529cae56b4"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-23-20","kanda":3,"kandaId":