se":22,"english":"The universal uproar filled that (entire) forest. Scared and terrified at the hubbub the rangers of the wood fle: to quarters free from noise; nor did they cast their eyes backward.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.554,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-24-24"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3023022","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"22e70a60c63fe2f97493225e0b6f07014432e3592e952a4d7112dd88b43afdc8","compact":"1f9487e4a3070e1f2c6961f58cebb58134312a2cd8acccd8802f6f09d1da4446","nasal":"1f9487e4a3070e1f2c6961f58cebb58134312a2cd8acccd8802f6f09d1da4446"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-23-23","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":23,"verse":23,"english":"And that army resembling the ocean, and rife with sounds, equipped with various weapons, with furious speed came towards Rāma.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.604,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-24-25"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3023023","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7e4abb3b8a0899218e8222d4aaa5d5c26bb36735fcaa51f2fc032bb673792004","compact":"43fc7c71b72f339534ec66f257509ea4aabf51d66b0adc998ca45fb198141d51","nasal":"31c234183c9c4fa0516f8180886c12a2531821662ca44f4509329415bdf5cc8f"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-23-24","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":23,"verse":24,"english":"And Rāma also versed in warfare, casting his eyes around, found the forces of Khara ready for fight. Another text:-The holder of Pinaka.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.79,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-24-26"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3023024","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9410d4c1fc195f9af7fc9e237d26d6ab518c1790fe16efa13c14c8c160617d63","compact":"772b502e5e8462d1535f34d6ab99cf679c1ceb642dde311206